WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.961
{\an8}<i>And now.</i> Hattie’s Tea Party.

2
00:00:02.962 --> 00:00:06.298
{\an8}<i>with your hostess with the mostest:
Hattie Tetch!</i>

3
00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:09.134
Good evening. Gotham.

4
00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:14.597
Crime. It's a plague in our city.
and no one seems to be looking for a cure.

5
00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:18.894
<i>Nightly gunfire and bloodshed
have become routine in Gotham.</i>

6
00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:20.730
<i>None of us are safe.</i>

7
00:00:21.147 --> 00:00:23.189
<i>Commissioner James Gordon
and his officers</i>

8
00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.442
<i>have turned our streets
into a war zone.</i>

9
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:35.869
<i>And matters are only made worse by
the interference of a masked outlaw</i>

10
00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:39.999
<i>whose true agenda remains unknown
to the good citizens of Gotham.</i>

11
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

12
00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:53.845
<i>And while we cower in our homes.</i>

13
00:00:53.846 --> 00:00:59.810
<i>the G.C.P.D. spends its time harassing one
of Gotham’s most esteemed businessmen.</i>

14
00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:04.647
If you’ve been following my coverage
of Rupert Thorne’s trial.

15
00:01:04.648 --> 00:01:08.568
then you know that the case
against him is gossamer thin.

16
00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:13.364
Rumor has it. D.A. Peter Mitchell
has found a surprise witness

17
00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:15.909
to bolster his flimsy prosecution.

18
00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:19.579
<i>But they don’t call me the Mad Hatter
of News for nothing.</i>

19
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.290
<i>I did get the name for you.
dear ones.</i>

20
00:01:22.291 --> 00:01:25.668
<i>Now. we can all hear
what surprising comments</i>

21
00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:31.424
<i>Thorne’s accountant. Julian Gregory. makes
when he’s flown to testify this week.</i>

22
00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:35.762
<i>Some of Mr. Gregory’s colleagues
refer to him as “Calendar Man”</i>

23
00:01:35.763 --> 00:01:39.724
<i>because of his eidetic memory
when it comes to dates and times.</i>

24
00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:43.354
<i>That should make it very easy for him
to remember the day that he was...</i>

25
00:01:46.607 --> 00:01:48.650
Is there a problem.
Mr. Thorne?

26
00:01:48.651 --> 00:01:53.363
Yeah. I need a new television.

27
00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:56.742
And Julian Gregory has to die.

28
00:02:35.364 --> 00:02:38.199
Are we certain that Gotham
International is out of the question?

29
00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.160
The D.A.’s office won’t put Gregory
on a commercial flight.

30
00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.705
Gordon will use one of
the smaller airports.

31
00:02:43.706 --> 00:02:45.915
I would think that
the Commissioner would simply

32
00:02:45.916 --> 00:02:47.959
tell you the whereabouts
of this accountant.

33
00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.796
I work alongside the police. Pennyworth.
That doesn't make me one of them.

34
00:02:51.797 --> 00:02:54.799
But with the professional relationship
you have with Barbara Gordon.

35
00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.594
her father should
extend more trust.

36
00:02:57.595 --> 00:03:01.222
Our goals might be the same.
but our methods never will be.

37
00:03:01.223 --> 00:03:04.767
Moldoff Airfield would definitely
suit the Commissioner’s needs.

38
00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:07.562
So would the Burnly County airstrip.

39
00:03:07.563 --> 00:03:10.231
Shall I investigate one
while you the other?

40
00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:12.984
No. I'm taking your advice.

41
00:03:12.985 --> 00:03:15.403
Oh? The father or the daughter?

42
00:03:15.404 --> 00:03:16.488
Barbara.

43
00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:21.159
Sir. if you truly haven’t earned
the Commissioner’s trust.

44
00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.620
he might not appreciate your attendance.

45
00:03:23.621 --> 00:03:27.166
I might be uninvited.
but that doesn't mean I'm unexpected.

46
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:39.260
Your guest is here. Mr. Thorne.

47
00:03:39.261 --> 00:03:40.679
Take a seat.

48
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:47.268
I'm hearing a lot of things
I don't like. Eddie.

49
00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:49.854
Things about how my business
is being handled.

50
00:03:49.855 --> 00:03:52.649
Mishandled by you.

51
00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.360
It's that damn Batman!

52
00:03:55.361 --> 00:04:00.365
-Every time we make a move. he...
-That lunatic is not top of the list.

53
00:04:00.366 --> 00:04:02.034
Who is at the top. Eddie?

54
00:04:03.077 --> 00:04:05.078
The accountant.

55
00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:06.829
Good. Eddie.

56
00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:11.709
It would also be good if tomorrow
he wasn't troubled with breathing anymore.

57
00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.753
Oh. I'll find him.

58
00:04:13.754 --> 00:04:18.132
If I gotta turn over every rock in Gotham.

59
00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:22.512
-He's already been found.
-You got a mole in the G.C.P.D.

60
00:04:22.513 --> 00:04:27.266
Diversify your portfolio. Eddie.
You diversify. you have options.

61
00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:31.980
Options. Yeah... I'll remember that.

62
00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:35.024
You know damn well this isn't fair.

63
00:04:35.025 --> 00:04:38.319
You put the bullet in Dent.
and I'm the one who loses his shield.

64
00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.781
Relax. You'll get your shield back. buddy.
I'm working on it.

65
00:04:41.782 --> 00:04:45.868
You been handing me that line for weeks.
and I’m fed up with it.

66
00:04:45.869 --> 00:04:48.997
I'm not the only one with skeletons.
Flass. If I don’t get...

67
00:04:48.998 --> 00:04:52.417
-Whoa. Where do you think you're going?
-Step aside. sister.

68
00:04:52.418 --> 00:04:55.628
This meeting is for
detectives only. officer.

69
00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:57.714
No uniforms.

70
00:04:57.715 --> 00:05:01.635
-Flass?
-Sorry. Sloppy Joe. Chain of command.

71
00:05:05.472 --> 00:05:10.393
Hattie Tetch is annoying. but she’s right.
The D.A.’s case is shaky.

72
00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:14.188
Julian Gregory is our last. best chance
to put Thorne away for good.

73
00:05:14.189 --> 00:05:18.401
We need to protect Gregory and clamp a lid
on every detail about this case.

74
00:05:18.402 --> 00:05:20.153
Thorne's broken every law in the book.

75
00:05:20.154 --> 00:05:22.196
how does this case come down
to one witness?

76
00:05:22.197 --> 00:05:24.741
Thorne's pockets are
as deep as his crimes.

77
00:05:24.742 --> 00:05:28.369
That makes putting him away harder.
but we need to get it done.

78
00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.039
It's our job to protect this city.
No one else's.

79
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:34.375
-Yeah. you and your bat buddy.
-Something to say. Flass?

80
00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:38.922
Absolutely not. sir. On the job. sir.
Protect this city.

81
00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:48.222
You're worthless!
Every one of you. Worthless.

82
00:05:48.223 --> 00:05:50.933
What about me. Eddie?
Am I worthless?

83
00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:53.478
Not now. baby. I'm workin'.

84
00:05:53.479 --> 00:05:55.522
Argh! You ruined my train of thought.

85
00:05:57.441 --> 00:05:59.817
You were tellin' 'em all
how worthless they are.

86
00:05:59.818 --> 00:06:02.153
Yeah. yeah. yeah. that's right.
Worthless!

87
00:06:02.154 --> 00:06:04.322
Every single one of ya.

88
00:06:04.323 --> 00:06:08.159
The Thorne Mob?
More like the Keystone Idiots!

89
00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.244
Tonight. that's over.

90
00:06:10.245 --> 00:06:13.915
Tonight. you're gonna
show me you got what it takes!

91
00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:16.293
Show me you're bona fide!

92
00:06:16.877 --> 00:06:19.462
-What's "bona fide"?
-Like this ring here.

93
00:06:19.463 --> 00:06:23.300
-Eddie got it for me. It's the real deal.
-Shut up!

94
00:06:24.176 --> 00:06:26.511
We run this town. see?

95
00:06:26.512 --> 00:06:29.597
We run it.
and we’re gonna keep running it.

96
00:06:29.598 --> 00:06:33.810
no matter what that sniveling accountant
squealing in court like a...

97
00:06:33.811 --> 00:06:36.437
A pig! A mouse?

98
00:06:43.695 --> 00:06:46.823
The squealer goes tonight. Get me?

99
00:06:46.824 --> 00:06:50.244
No mistakes. No excuses.

100
00:06:51.578 --> 00:06:54.581
In the dirt.

101
00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.049
-This is Gordon.
<i>-Barbara.</i>

102
00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:09.762
Oh. hi. Let me guess.
you need some legal help?

103
00:07:09.763 --> 00:07:11.430
<i>I need information.</i>

104
00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:14.308
{\an8}Moldoff Airfield
or Burnly County airstrip.

105
00:07:14.309 --> 00:07:16.562
{\an8}where is your father
meeting the accountant?

106
00:07:17.062 --> 00:07:18.521
Right. Of course.

107
00:07:18.522 --> 00:07:21.816
Unfortunately. my father doesn’t
tell me case details.

108
00:07:21.817 --> 00:07:24.987
He’s in danger. Barbara.
Withholding this isn’t helping him.

109
00:07:25.904 --> 00:07:29.615
Okay. Fine. I guess. in the past.
he’s used Moldoff. but...

110
00:07:35.581 --> 00:07:37.540
-You made a good speech.
-Thanks.

111
00:07:37.541 --> 00:07:39.293
And didn’t mention the Batman.

112
00:07:39.835 --> 00:07:41.502
The Batman is an asset.

113
00:07:41.503 --> 00:07:46.716
I appreciate what he does. but I won’t
rely on him to do this department’s job.

114
00:07:46.717 --> 00:07:48.467
I’m not built that way.

115
00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:51.555
-Neither am I.
-I know. I count on that.

116
00:08:03.025 --> 00:08:04.817
Oh! Oh! Here’s another one.

117
00:08:04.818 --> 00:08:07.987
What do James Polk and Warren G. Harding
have in common?

118
00:08:07.988 --> 00:08:13.034
-I don't know. both were presidents?
-Same birthday! November 2nd. Scorpios!

119
00:08:13.035 --> 00:08:14.452
What are the odds?

120
00:08:24.421 --> 00:08:26.255
Whoa. whoa!

121
00:08:48.028 --> 00:08:50.822
Whoo!

122
00:08:52.741 --> 00:08:55.285
Die. squealer! Die!

123
00:09:27.401 --> 00:09:29.277
Come on. Eddie. Let's get outta here.

124
00:09:36.785 --> 00:09:38.327
Let go. ya freak!

125
00:09:38.328 --> 00:09:40.997
I got nothing to...

126
00:09:48.505 --> 00:09:52.508
Eddie. you didn’t have to do that.
Jimmy woulda never squealed.

127
00:09:52.509 --> 00:09:56.262
That’s how a secret
stays secret. Dez.

128
00:09:56.263 --> 00:09:59.765
Yeah. sure.
but when Mr. Thorne finds out...

129
00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:02.143
But Thorne ain’t gonna find out

130
00:10:02.144 --> 00:10:07.398
because that accountant’s gonna be in
the dirt before anybody tells him. Yeah?

131
00:10:07.399 --> 00:10:11.610
Okay. Okay. All I'm saying is.
how you gonna do it. Eddie?

132
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:12.988
Don't worry about it.

133
00:10:13.697 --> 00:10:15.699
I know a guy.

134
00:10:22.497 --> 00:10:24.499
Dad told me you saved the accountant.

135
00:10:27.419 --> 00:10:30.463
Now I need to know
where your father is keeping him.

136
00:10:30.464 --> 00:10:33.258
Or you can just call him.
ask him yourself.

137
00:10:34.426 --> 00:10:37.803
He can’t give me that information
without compromising himself.

138
00:10:37.804 --> 00:10:40.014
But I can? Of course. I can.

139
00:10:40.015 --> 00:10:44.227
I’m Barbara Gordon. public defender.
I’m always compromised.

140
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:48.439
Protecting Julian Gregory
is all that matters right now.

141
00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.066
I don't know where he is.

142
00:10:50.067 --> 00:10:51.984
-You can find out.
-Maybe.

143
00:10:51.985 --> 00:10:54.904
If I cross a bunch of lines
that I'm never going to cross.

144
00:10:54.905 --> 00:10:57.365
I won't spy on my father.

145
00:10:57.366 --> 00:11:00.368
-You can trust me.
-I do.

146
00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:04.247
I trust you'll find him on your own.
Without using me.

147
00:11:12.923 --> 00:11:16.217
You know why you're here.
I need to get to the truth.

148
00:11:16.218 --> 00:11:17.385
Sir?

149
00:11:17.386 --> 00:11:19.720
Thorne knew when
and where Gregory was landing.

150
00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:22.431
If we have a leak in this department.
I need you to plug it.

151
00:11:22.432 --> 00:11:25.727
Sir. if there's a leak in the department.
we both know that it's F...

152
00:11:26.645 --> 00:11:28.354
I thought you wanted to see me.
Commissioner.

153
00:11:28.355 --> 00:11:31.607
But if you’re giving Montoya one
of your little pep talks. I can always...

154
00:11:31.608 --> 00:11:34.402
Detective Montoya
is your new partner. Flass.

155
00:11:34.403 --> 00:11:35.611
Sir?!

156
00:11:35.612 --> 00:11:38.406
Great. She’s more of a looker
than the last one.

157
00:11:38.407 --> 00:11:40.867
Another thing. Montoya’s the lead.

158
00:11:42.369 --> 00:11:44.370
I want the two of you on Gregory.

159
00:11:44.371 --> 00:11:47.707
Get him to the Chandler Arms
and sit on him until he testifies.

160
00:11:54.172 --> 00:11:55.173
Montoya.

161
00:11:56.091 --> 00:11:57.426
Watch your back.

162
00:12:02.472 --> 00:12:04.390
What you got for us. Strange?

163
00:12:04.391 --> 00:12:08.602
Professor. please.
I worked long and hard for that title.

164
00:12:08.603 --> 00:12:12.023
-Mister... Nygma. was it?
-Eddie's fine.

165
00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:15.068
The things I make are expensive.

166
00:12:15.735 --> 00:12:18.279
But the knowledge to make
them untraceable?

167
00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:21.824
-There’s no upper price on that.
-Understood.

168
00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:27.205
When we get rid of the Batman.
Gotham will be ours.

169
00:12:29.332 --> 00:12:30.750
This way.

170
00:12:38.592 --> 00:12:40.342
And this is?

171
00:12:40.343 --> 00:12:44.096
Power. Strength. Aggression.

172
00:12:44.097 --> 00:12:50.437
All beyond the limits of any man.
Or rodent. flying or otherwise.

173
00:12:52.022 --> 00:12:55.691
-Price?
-Consider it a field test.

174
00:12:55.692 --> 00:12:59.612
The Batman is an interesting
environmental hurdle.

175
00:12:59.613 --> 00:13:04.201
I would like to see how my formula
does in a... human trial.

176
00:13:04.951 --> 00:13:09.956
Y’know. what. prof?
I definitely wanna see that too.

177
00:13:24.429 --> 00:13:25.889
Towel.

178
00:13:27.682 --> 00:13:29.684
Towel. goddammit!

179
00:13:38.693 --> 00:13:42.821
If you’re here to apologize for
slicing my ear. don’t worry about it.

180
00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:47.035
It healed up good as new.
It’s like you never even touched me.

181
00:13:49.621 --> 00:13:53.582
Nothing to say. Strong and silent. huh?

182
00:13:53.583 --> 00:13:57.295
Is this supposed
to turn my spine to jelly?

183
00:13:57.963 --> 00:14:00.297
You’ve got it backwards. freak.

184
00:14:00.298 --> 00:14:03.760
If you’re here.
you’re the one who’s running scared.

185
00:14:05.136 --> 00:14:07.304
I’m gonna beat this rap.

186
00:14:07.305 --> 00:14:11.518
And when I do. I am going to make it my
mission in life to burn...

187
00:14:13.186 --> 00:14:16.647
Go on! Do it!

188
00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:23.988
I knew it. You don’t have the stones
for the real dirty work.

189
00:14:23.989 --> 00:14:25.948
That’s why I’m gonna win.

190
00:14:27.492 --> 00:14:31.245
Gordon thinks that safe house
of his is Fort Knox.

191
00:14:31.246 --> 00:14:32.871
He’s dreaming.

192
00:14:32.872 --> 00:14:37.042
I can put my finger on Gregory anytime.
anywhere. Bank on it.

193
00:14:37.043 --> 00:14:41.298
The accountant has seen his last sunrise.

194
00:14:46.678 --> 00:14:51.807
You’re going to burn. freak.
Bank on that too. You will burn!

195
00:14:53.518 --> 00:14:56.895
Pennyworth. which G.C.P.D. safe houses
are still active?

196
00:14:56.896 --> 00:14:59.189
<i>The Adams Garage.
the Chandler Arms.</i>

197
00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:01.066
<i>and the Ward Street Church.</i>

198
00:15:01.067 --> 00:15:03.027
Three stops. Done.

199
00:15:07.782 --> 00:15:12.912
Look at that squealer.
Just like Rapunzel hiding in her tower.

200
00:15:14.289 --> 00:15:17.124
So what's the plan?
Do we shoot our way in?

201
00:15:17.125 --> 00:15:18.584
No. Dez.

202
00:15:18.585 --> 00:15:22.338
This job calls for something much bigger.

203
00:15:24.174 --> 00:15:26.300
And a helluva lot messier.

204
00:15:26.301 --> 00:15:29.846
-Okay. What are we gonna use?
-Not what. Dez.

205
00:15:30.263 --> 00:15:32.973
Whom.

206
00:15:56.206 --> 00:15:59.917
Beautiful! You’re beautiful!

207
00:15:59.918 --> 00:16:03.004
Now. what do we need to do?

208
00:16:03.755 --> 00:16:07.091
Kill the squealer.

209
00:16:07.092 --> 00:16:12.680
Calm? Calm? How can I stay calm?
Thorne can find me here!

210
00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:14.223
He can find me anywhere!

211
00:16:14.224 --> 00:16:17.686
Relax. Detective Montoya here
is on the case.

212
00:16:18.395 --> 00:16:22.064
We've kept this location a secret. Julian.
You'll be fine.

213
00:16:22.065 --> 00:16:24.526
What the hell?

214
00:16:51.928 --> 00:16:55.973
Time to die. squealer.

215
00:16:55.974 --> 00:16:57.058
Take it down!

216
00:17:12.699 --> 00:17:16.368
This is Montoya. I need backup
at Chandler Arms! Now!

217
00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:20.415
You.

218
00:17:23.126 --> 00:17:24.835
What the hell are you doing?

219
00:17:33.136 --> 00:17:35.138
Move your ass. Calendar Man!

220
00:17:50.904 --> 00:17:54.616
Kill the squealer.

221
00:17:55.742 --> 00:17:56.742
Move it!

222
00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:18.508
On February 3rd.
I did inform Mr. Thorne

223
00:20:18.509 --> 00:20:22.220
that the filings were inaccurate
and. uh... Unlawful.

224
00:20:22.221 --> 00:20:23.639
And his response?

225
00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:28.936
Mr. Thorne said.
“The law is whatever I decide it is.”

226
00:20:31.105 --> 00:20:32.815
Your witness.

227
00:20:34.734 --> 00:20:39.363
Your honor. the defense moves
for a complete dismissal of all charges.

228
00:20:39.364 --> 00:20:43.241
The prosecution’s case is nothing more
than a collection of tainted evidence

229
00:20:43.242 --> 00:20:48.790
brought to us by a police department
famous for its corruption and ineptitude.

230
00:20:54.045 --> 00:20:59.508
The court has reached a verdict.

231
00:20:59.509 --> 00:21:02.928
I’m prepared to rule this case a...

232
00:21:02.929 --> 00:21:04.805
<i>As this reporter predicted.</i>

233
00:21:04.806 --> 00:21:08.850
<i>the case against Rupert Thorne
was completely dismissed.</i>

234
00:21:08.851 --> 00:21:11.937
<i>Despite the best efforts
of D.A. Peter Mitchell.</i>

235
00:21:11.938 --> 00:21:15.065
<i>Commissioner Gordon and our circus
of a police department.</i>

236
00:21:15.066 --> 00:21:18.736
<i>the day was overwhelmingly
Rupert Thorne’s.</i>

237
00:21:24.158 --> 00:21:25.827
-You okay. Dad?
-No.

238
00:21:26.494 --> 00:21:29.871
-I'm far from okay.
-Thorne got to the judge.

239
00:21:29.872 --> 00:21:31.665
We should've seen it coming.

240
00:21:31.666 --> 00:21:34.001
Yeah. but you didn't.
because you're chumps.

241
00:21:34.002 --> 00:21:36.837
You keep thinking Gotham's
gonna do right someday.

242
00:21:36.838 --> 00:21:39.297
You need to get as far away from me
as possible. Flass.

243
00:21:39.298 --> 00:21:43.219
Wake up. Nemo.
This ain't dreamland.

244
00:21:44.846 --> 00:21:47.305
The energy here is electric.

245
00:21:47.306 --> 00:21:51.977
Thorne’s exoneration symbolizes
the start of Gotham’s next chapter.

246
00:21:51.978 --> 00:21:54.855
-Perhaps now some civility...
-Here they come!

247
00:21:54.856 --> 00:21:56.148
Oh! Here he is!

248
00:21:56.149 --> 00:21:58.316
-Here they are!
-Mr. Thorne!

249
00:22:01.279 --> 00:22:03.990
Mr. Thorne. how does
it feel to be exonerated?

250
00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:06.074
I hate this.

251
00:22:06.075 --> 00:22:11.080
Thorne won this round. but if he thinks
this fight is over. he’s dead wrong.

252
00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:17.544
Mr. Thorne. do you have a few words
you can share on this glorious day?

253
00:22:17.545 --> 00:22:19.087
Nice hat.

254
00:22:21.841 --> 00:22:27.597
Rupert Thorne. the brightest light
in Gotham is free to shine once more.

255
00:22:32.518 --> 00:22:34.979
-Ouch.
-I'm terribly sorry. sir.

256
00:22:35.938 --> 00:22:37.315
Incompetent.

257
00:22:42.945 --> 00:22:47.574
-I knew we'd beat 'em. Dad.
-We didn’t beat them. son. We own them.

258
00:22:47.575 --> 00:22:52.746
Always keep a diversified portfolio.
my boy! Diversify. and you can’t lose!

259
00:22:52.747 --> 00:22:59.419
Every goddamn
one of those suckers belongs to me.

260
00:23:02.965 --> 00:23:06.010
Dad? What's so funny?

261
00:23:10.181 --> 00:23:12.391
Dad. cut it out! You're scaring me.

262
00:23:13.601 --> 00:23:17.562
Dad. stop! Stop laughing! Please!

263
00:23:35.581 --> 00:23:37.959
Barbara?

264
00:23:38.793 --> 00:23:41.212
-Honey. why did you...
-Okay.

265
00:23:43.047 --> 00:23:47.009
You two need to talk.
And you need to do it without me.

266
00:23:57.270 --> 00:23:59.980
Some in Gotham called
a so-called Batman

267
00:23:59.981 --> 00:24:01.274
a hero.

268
00:24:01.941 --> 00:24:03.275
But I ask you.

269
00:24:03.276 --> 00:24:05.694
who appointed this anonymous vigilante

270
00:24:05.695 --> 00:24:09.030
judge. jury and executioner
of Gotham City?

271
00:24:10.324 --> 00:24:12.034
Murder. Robbery.

272
00:24:12.326 --> 00:24:14.703
More in the last three weeks
than in all of last year.

273
00:24:14.704 --> 00:24:17.373
You know. we just might crack this
working together.

274
00:24:18.332 --> 00:24:21.377
Right. You always work alone.

275
00:24:22.003 --> 00:24:24.713
I see our Mr. Riddler is escalating.

276
00:24:24.714 --> 00:24:27.383
Now. it's a party!

277
00:24:28.009 --> 00:24:30.219
One of Thorne's lieutenants
making his own moves.

278
00:24:30.678 --> 00:24:31.845
I'm running things.

279
00:24:34.015 --> 00:24:35.557
I really miss Harleen.

280
00:24:35.558 --> 00:24:38.018
If they'd found her body.
at least we could grieve.

281
00:24:38.019 --> 00:24:39.437
It's like she's still out there.

282
00:24:39.896 --> 00:24:42.147
So. the last time we talked...

283
00:24:42.148 --> 00:24:43.315
You tried to kill me.

284
00:24:43.316 --> 00:24:45.483
Fair. I did.

285
00:24:45.484 --> 00:24:47.152
But not very hard.

286
00:24:49.614 --> 00:24:52.158
Be careful out there. Barb.
Storm's getting rough.

287
00:24:52.617 --> 00:24:54.327
Well. well...

288
00:24:54.827 --> 00:24:56.620
what do we have here?

289
00:24:56.621 --> 00:24:58.496
The whole city's on the verge of panic.

290
00:25:03.377 --> 00:25:05.712
Everything this lunatic has done.

291
00:25:05.713 --> 00:25:07.465
has been to destroy Gotham.

292
00:25:10.051 --> 00:25:12.010
We need you to stop him.

293
00:25:12.011 --> 00:25:14.054
I want him dead. do you get me?

294
00:25:14.055 --> 00:25:16.348
Dead! Dead!

295
00:25:16.349 --> 00:25:18.309
Dead. dead. dead. dead!

296
00:25:20.228 --> 00:25:22.938
Strike him down. my children.

297
00:25:26.067 --> 00:25:27.609
We are losing this fight.

298
00:25:27.610 --> 00:25:29.194
Not a fight anymore. boss.

299
00:25:29.195 --> 00:25:31.489
This new guy's making it war.

300
00:25:32.114 --> 00:25:33.741
Good evening. Gotham.

301
00:25:34.408 --> 00:25:35.909
It falls at dawn.

302
00:25:38.537 --> 00:25:39.955
All of you...

303
00:25:44.293 --> 00:25:45.252
will die.

303
